WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.860
Sometimes blank strings and NULL represent the same
business state If that

00:00:05.873 --> 00:00:12.190
rule is documented NULLIF can convert a
blank-after-trimming string into NULL This

00:00:12.203 --> 00:00:17.375
can make later logic easier because one missing
representation is easier to handle than several

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:22.336
But do this only when blank truly means missing for
that field
